{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZjsV2E8daWGNGbkNbKaLK","type":"tool_result","content":".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:35:- R1: A spec shall be able to declare `### Accepted limits` entries with stable ids (`L<N>`), each naming the assumption and why it is accepted.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:38:- R4: `lint-spec --ready-check` shall require accepted limits to be justified and the ADR, when present, to reference them.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:81:### Accepted limits\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:86:A spec section `### Accepted limits` with `- L<N>: <assumption>. Accepted because <reason>.` entries. The review plan and the bundle seal them as `accepted_limits` (omitted when none, so every other plan and bundle keeps its digest). A draft finding may carry `limit`; the attestation records it with disposition `within-limit`. Brief template `review-brief/11`. `lint-spec --ready-check` checks the section.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:112:A finding inside a declared limit is neither an open finding nor an accepted risk: it gets its own disposition, `within-limit`, which does not block an approval whatever its severity, requires a sealed limit and a reason, and records the limit's id. Accepted risks keep their severity bound; a limit is the spec's statement of scope, decided before the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:129:- 2026-11-25: implemented R1–R4: `ParseAcceptedLimits`, the plan and bundle `accepted_limits`, the draft `limit` and the `within-limit` disposition, `review-brief/11` and the ready check. Each has a test that fails with it mutated out; the first digest test survived because the spec edit changed the scope digest too, and now compares the plan's digest with and without the limits.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:134:- 2026-11-25: review round 5 (rrn-9f6867b3c3e42377): N1, a whitespace-only reason of a `within-limit` finding is refused; N2, the ready check fails closed on an ADR directory or file it cannot read, keeping the absent-directory case. Both have tests that fail with them mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:157:Specs declare accepted limits; the review plan and bundle seal them; `review-brief/11` lists them and tells the reviewer to classify a finding inside one with `limit`; the attestation records it `within-limit`, which does not block an approval; `lint-spec --ready-check` requires each limit to say why it is accepted and an ADR citing the spec to name it.\nPOSE.md:1078:[Omitted long matching line]\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1065:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:[Omitted long matching line]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"0e6708aa-a51c-45f3-8674-c14781df53ab","timestamp":"2026-11-26T00:20:51.646Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":".pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:35:- R1: A spec shall be able to declare `### Accepted limits` entries with stable ids (`L<N>`), each naming the assumption and why it is accepted.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:38:- R4: `lint-spec --ready-check` shall require accepted limits to be justified and the ADR, when present, to reference them.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:81:### Accepted limits\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:86:A spec section `### Accepted limits` with `- L<N>: <assumption>. Accepted because <reason>.` entries. The review plan and the bundle seal them as `accepted_limits` (omitted when none, so every other plan and bundle keeps its digest). A draft finding may carry `limit`; the attestation records it with disposition `within-limit`. Brief template `review-brief/11`. `lint-spec --ready-check` checks the section.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:112:A finding inside a declared limit is neither an open finding nor an accepted risk: it gets its own disposition, `within-limit`, which does not block an approval whatever its severity, requires a sealed limit and a reason, and records the limit's id. Accepted risks keep their severity bound; a limit is the spec's statement of scope, decided before the review.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:129:- 2026-11-25: implemented R1–R4: `ParseAcceptedLimits`, the plan and bundle `accepted_limits`, the draft `limit` and the `within-limit` disposition, `review-brief/11` and the ready check. Each has a test that fails with it mutated out; the first digest test survived because the spec edit changed the scope digest too, and now compares the plan's digest with and without the limits.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:134:- 2026-11-25: review round 5 (rrn-9f6867b3c3e42377): N1, a whitespace-only reason of a `within-limit` finding is refused; N2, the ready check fails closed on an ADR directory or file it cannot read, keeping the absent-directory case. Both have tests that fail with them mutated out.\n.pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-declared-threat-model.md:157:Specs declare accepted limits; the review plan and bundle seal them; `review-brief/11` lists them and tells the reviewer to classify a finding inside one with `limit`; the attestation records it `within-limit`, which does not block an approval; `lint-spec --ready-check` requires each limit to say why it is accepted and an ADR citing the spec to name it.\nPOSE.md:1078:[Omitted long matching line]\nlocales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md:1065:[Omitted long matching line]\npose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:1075:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":12,"totalLines":12},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CZjsV2E8daWGNGbkNbKaLK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
