{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChQcoUidcTvjy3csLJuNd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01So9v8KKCA7GZz7M9aKxPds","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":68,\"summary\":\"A limit wrapped over several Markdown lines is silently cut at its first line: any line not starting with a dash is skipped. A probe with \\\"- L1: An escape. Accepted because a shim covers it\\\" followed by the indented line \\\"only on Linux and only for children.\\\" parsed with no problem and sealed only the first line, so the qualifier that narrows the limit is lost from the plan, the digests and the brief, and within-limit is judged against a broader limit than the spec declares. Read the continuation lines into the entry, or refuse a wrapped entry, with a test.\",\"action\":\"Join continuation lines into the limit text, or report them as a ready-check problem and refuse to seal a truncated limit.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":65,\"summary\":\"The parser ignores Markdown fences and HTML comments: an example Accepted limits section inside a fenced block or inside a comment is parsed with no problem and sealed as a real limit (probe confirmed both). A commented entry is hidden in the rendered spec yet can classify a finding of any severity; the brief does list it.\",\"action\":\"Skip fenced blocks and HTML comments when reading the section.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\",\"line\":142,\"summary\":\"review-brief/11 contradicts itself and the engine: rule (i) still says an approving draft leaves open every follow-up without action, owner and review_by and accepts only low severity, while the Accepted limits section and reviewFindingDecisionBlockers let a follow-up with a sealed limit through without them at any severity. The list of finding fields in the return step also omits limit.\",\"action\":\"State the within-limit exception in rule (i) and name limit among the finding fields, under a new template version.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":1211,\"summary\":\"An ADR cites a spec when it merely contains its slug as a substring, so an ADR about a longer slug (pose-review versus pose-review-readiness-before-seal) is taken to cite the shorter spec and the ready check then demands the shorter spec limits in it. Same shape as the L10 versus L1 defect fixed in round 1.\",\"action\":\"Match the slug as a whole token, with a test using a prefix slug.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_outcomes.go\",\"line\":445,\"summary\":\"The new within-limit disposition has no bucket: governance outcomes count the finding as observed and as an intervention but in none of accepted_risk, resolved, wont_fix or open, so the stats no longer add up and classified findings are invisible there. The text output of review-check and closeout-check does not show them either (only the JSON of review-check carries the findings).\",\"action\":\"Count within-limit findings in their own field and show it in governance stats.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":49,\"limit\":\"L1\",\"summary\":\"Carried from R7-N1: the lexical gate accepts placeholder text such as \\\"X. Y. Accepted because z w.\\\" since it counts letter runs. It falls inside L1: the check is a format gate, the implementer writes the limit, and the sealed brief shows its text for the reviewer to judge and dispute.\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R7-N1\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:40-49 is unchanged in this respect; recorded again as N6 within the sealed limit L1, as that finding falls inside it.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R7-N2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"lintspec.go:1244-1256 readADRBounded does Lstat, requires a regular file and reads through ReadReviewAdapterFile (O_NOFOLLOW, O_NONBLOCK on Unix, 1 MiB bound, identity recheck); go test ./internal/cli -run ReadyCheckJudges passed, including the link to /dev/zero. Residual not raised: a linked .pose/adr directory is still followed, but only bounded regular files are read and no content is echoed.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"Read the spec, accepted_limits.go, the diffs of lintspec.go, review_plan.go, review_bundle.go, review_conclusions.go, review_rounds.go, review_closeout.go, review_brief.go, the template digests, the new and changed tests and both manuals; followed within-limit through draft parsing, attestation building, run conclusion matching, decision blockers, criterion reuse, legacy attempt evaluation, governance outcomes, obligations and the CLI check outputs; checked plan and bundle digest compatibility; probed the parser with a go test overlay kept in TMPDIR; ran focused tests (pass), the planned pose tools, and the full pose and cli packages plus module validate, whose failures seen come from the sandbox (path ownership, sockets, network, file mode) and not from these changes. The checkout stayed clean.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1 and L2 against code. L2 holds: accepted limits enter digestReviewPlan and reviewBundlePlanDigest. L1 is justified for how broad or weak a limit is written, not for the engine cutting it (N1). review-check warns the sealed evidence is current by provenance rather than run on the subject head; local focused tests of the scope passed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds pure parsing, digest fields and a bounded file read; no shared state or new goroutine in production code.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Unsealed limit and blank reason are refused with named blockers; ADR reads are bounded and fail closed. The parser gap is recorded under correctness.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N5\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals name the finding and limit; the attestation records limit and reason. The stats gap is N5.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\"rationale\":\"accepted_limits and limit are omitempty in plan, bundle, draft and finding and in both plan digests; the bundle digest test compares with the earlier struct; earlier brief templates render without the new section and the digest tests pass.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"D1 and D2 address the cause, no place to declare an assumed environment: limits are sealed from the spec, listed in the brief and judged from the bundle, with a separate disposition that needs a sealed id. The design assessment reports no structural delta.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The scope change sets match R1 to R4 and the declared artifacts; no cap on rounds was added. The brief template file also carries earlier versions belonging to other specs in the range.\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"within-limit requires an id sealed in the bundle and a non-blank reason; a run attestation must match the draft; the manual attest syntax cannot set a limit; brief text is flattened by quoteLedgerText; ADR reads do not follow file links. Fidelity of the sealed text is N1 and N2.\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"One section, one optional field and one disposition is close to the smallest way to classify findings; an accepted-risk reuse would have lifted its severity bound. The choice fails if limits cannot be read faithfully, which N1 shows needs fixing.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; warnings only seen, 1005 findings reported.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-9ad64c4729c340ef\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist; three medium gaps about unobserved HTTP consumers.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Scan reports INCOMPLETE: two older spec files could not be read.\"},' '{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; not terminal before an attestation.\"},' '{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; not approved before an attestation.\"},' '{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, zero findings.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The unscoped command was not rerun here; the verdict rests on sealed evidence. See the module run, which failed in this sandbox.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The local rerun FAILED (test and several integration checks, one timeout) on sandbox restrictions seen in its output: foreign ownership of /home and /var/tmp, denied network, runtime sockets and file mode, in code outside this change. Passed rests on the sealed evidence only.\"}' ']}' '```' > \"$TMPDIR/final.md\" && cat \"$TMPDIR/final.md\" | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1399,"cache_read_input_tokens":211230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1399},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"c28b7317-546e-437e-9a3a-53333421c2b7","timestamp":"2026-11-26T00:48:06.863Z","request_id":"req_011ChQcoUXUdrk2TSmj2AGTy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01So9v8KKCA7GZz7M9aKxPds":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":68,\"summary\":\"A limit wrapped over several Markdown lines is silently cut at its first line: any line not starting with a dash is skipped. A probe with \\\"- L1: An escape. Accepted because a shim covers it\\\" followed by the indented line \\\"only on Linux and only for children.\\\" parsed with no problem and sealed only the first line, so the qualifier that narrows the limit is lost from the plan, the digests and the brief, and within-limit is judged against a broader limit than the spec declares. Read the continuation lines into the entry, or refuse a wrapped entry, with a test.\",\"action\":\"Join continuation lines into the limit text, or report them as a ready-check problem and refuse to seal a truncated limit.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":65,\"summary\":\"The parser ignores Markdown fences and HTML comments: an example Accepted limits section inside a fenced block or inside a comment is parsed with no problem and sealed as a real limit (probe confirmed both). A commented entry is hidden in the rendered spec yet can classify a finding of any severity; the brief does list it.\",\"action\":\"Skip fenced blocks and HTML comments when reading the section.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\",\"line\":142,\"summary\":\"review-brief/11 contradicts itself and the engine: rule (i) still says an approving draft leaves open every follow-up without action, owner and review_by and accepts only low severity, while the Accepted limits section and reviewFindingDecisionBlockers let a follow-up with a sealed limit through without them at any severity. The list of finding fields in the return step also omits limit.\",\"action\":\"State the within-limit exception in rule (i) and name limit among the finding fields, under a new template version.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\",\"line\":1211,\"summary\":\"An ADR cites a spec when it merely contains its slug as a substring, so an ADR about a longer slug (pose-review versus pose-review-readiness-before-seal) is taken to cite the shorter spec and the ready check then demands the shorter spec limits in it. Same shape as the L10 versus L1 defect fixed in round 1.\",\"action\":\"Match the slug as a whole token, with a test using a prefix slug.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_outcomes.go\",\"line\":445,\"summary\":\"The new within-limit disposition has no bucket: governance outcomes count the finding as observed and as an intervention but in none of accepted_risk, resolved, wont_fix or open, so the stats no longer add up and classified findings are invisible there. The text output of review-check and closeout-check does not show them either (only the JSON of review-check carries the findings).\",\"action\":\"Count within-limit findings in their own field and show it in governance stats.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N6\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\"line\":49,\"limit\":\"L1\",\"summary\":\"Carried from R7-N1: the lexical gate accepts placeholder text such as \\\"X. Y. Accepted because z w.\\\" since it counts letter runs. It falls inside L1: the check is a format gate, the implementer writes the limit, and the sealed brief shows its text for the reviewer to judge and dispute.\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R7-N1\",\"status\":\"superseded\",\"evidence\":\"accepted_limits.go:40-49 is unchanged in this respect; recorded again as N6 within the sealed limit L1, as that finding falls inside it.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R7-N2\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"lintspec.go:1244-1256 readADRBounded does Lstat, requires a regular file and reads through ReadReviewAdapterFile (O_NOFOLLOW, O_NONBLOCK on Unix, 1 MiB bound, identity recheck); go test ./internal/cli -run ReadyCheckJudges passed, including the link to /dev/zero. Residual not raised: a linked .pose/adr directory is still followed, but only bounded regular files are read and no content is echoed.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"Read the spec, accepted_limits.go, the diffs of lintspec.go, review_plan.go, review_bundle.go, review_conclusions.go, review_rounds.go, review_closeout.go, review_brief.go, the template digests, the new and changed tests and both manuals; followed within-limit through draft parsing, attestation building, run conclusion matching, decision blockers, criterion reuse, legacy attempt evaluation, governance outcomes, obligations and the CLI check outputs; checked plan and bundle digest compatibility; probed the parser with a go test overlay kept in TMPDIR; ran focused tests (pass), the planned pose tools, and the full pose and cli packages plus module validate, whose failures seen come from the sandbox (path ownership, sockets, network, file mode) and not from these changes. The checkout stayed clean.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Checked L1 and L2 against code. L2 holds: accepted limits enter digestReviewPlan and reviewBundlePlanDigest. L1 is justified for how broad or weak a limit is written, not for the engine cutting it (N1). review-check warns the sealed evidence is current by provenance rather than run on the subject head; local focused tests of the scope passed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The change adds pure parsing, digest fields and a bounded file read; no shared state or new goroutine in production code.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Unsealed limit and blank reason are refused with named blockers; ADR reads are bounded and fail closed. The parser gap is recorded under correctness.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N5\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Refusals name the finding and limit; the attestation records limit and reason. The stats gap is N5.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-brief-templates-are-immutable-integration\",\"rationale\":\"accepted_limits and limit are omitempty in plan, bundle, draft and finding and in both plan digests; the bundle digest test compares with the earlier struct; earlier brief templates render without the new section and the digest tests pass.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"D1 and D2 address the cause, no place to declare an assumed environment: limits are sealed from the spec, listed in the brief and judged from the bundle, with a separate disposition that needs a sealed id. The design assessment reports no structural delta.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The scope change sets match R1 to R4 and the declared artifacts; no cap on rounds was added. The brief template file also carries earlier versions belonging to other specs in the range.\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"within-limit requires an id sealed in the bundle and a non-blank reason; a run attestation must match the draft; the manual attest syntax cannot set a limit; brief text is flattened by quoteLedgerText; ADR reads do not follow file links. Fidelity of the sealed text is N1 and N2.\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"One section, one optional field and one disposition is close to the smallest way to classify findings; an accepted-risk reuse would have lifted its severity bound. The choice fails if limits cannot be read faithfully, which N1 shows needs fixing.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0; warnings only seen, 1005 findings reported.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-9ad64c4729c340ef\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist; three medium gaps about unobserved HTTP consumers.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"Scan reports INCOMPLETE: two older spec files could not be read.\"},' '{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; not terminal before an attestation.\"},' '{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; not approved before an attestation.\"},' '{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},' '{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0, zero findings.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The unscoped command was not rerun here; the verdict rests on sealed evidence. See the module run, which failed in this sandbox.\"},' '{\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The local rerun FAILED (test and several integration checks, one timeout) on sandbox restrictions seen in its output: foreign ownership of /home and /var/tmp, denied network, runtime sockets and file mode, in code outside this change. Passed rests on the sealed evidence only.\"}' ']}' '```' > \"$TMPDIR/final.md\" && cat \"$TMPDIR/final.md\" | \"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -","timeout":300000}}}
